Aim
To simulate mobile users moving across a multi-cell LTE/5G NR network in OMNeT++ (INET with Simu5G) and observe the handover process and its effect on traffic.
Detailed Algorithm
1.  Install OMNeT++ 6.x, INET and the matching Simu5G version; import them into the IDE and build.
2.  Copy a multi-cell example network from Simu5G (for example the X2/handover or multi-cell NR example) as MultiCellHandover. The topology has three base stations (eNodeB/gNodeB) about 500 m apart, a core network (UPF/PGW), a server and several UEs.
3.  In omnetpp.ini give each UE LinearMobility so that it travels across all three cells at constant speed.
4.  Enable handover in the UEs and base stations and enable the X2 (or Xn) interface between neighbouring cells.
5.  Install a downlink UDP stream from the server to every UE (UdpBasicApp at the server, UdpSink at the UE).
6.  Run with the Qtenv graphical runtime; watch the UE move and the serving cell change. Enable module logging to see the handover messages.
7.  Record the handover instants, serving cell versus time and the throughput of the UE; view them in the Analysis Tool.
8.  Repeat with UE speeds of 5, 20 and 40 m/s and compare the handover count and packet loss.
